cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, cite the repository version and preserve the source-data citations recorded by each analysis or case study."
type: software
title: "Materials Characterization Analyzer"
authors:
  - name: "jhin0410-lgtm"
version: 0.10.0
date-released: 2026-08-01
repository-code: "https://github.com/jhin0410-lgtm/materials-characterization-analyzer"
url: "https://github.com/jhin0410-lgtm/materials-characterization-analyzer"
license: BSD-3-Clause
abstract: >-
  A provenance-aware Python command-line toolkit for cautious baseline analysis,
  checksum-bound public real-data case studies, and reproducible output generation
  across XRD, SEM, EDS, Raman, TEM, SAED, XPS, FTIR, TGA, and DSC characterization
  workflows. The software separates software validation from scientific validation
  and does not automatically confirm phases, compounds, chemical states, functional
  groups, reactions, mechanisms, quantitative composition, segmentation validity,
  raw-image identity, parent-image independence, pixel calibration, or physical
  particle dimensions.
keywords:
  - materials science
  - materials characterization
  - provenance
  - XRD
  - SEM
  - EDS
  - Raman
  - TEM
  - SAED
  - XPS
  - FTIR
  - TGA
  - DSC
